From: Incari GmbH <>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:51:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3568: build without lib/libxbc and lib/sha512.c

Do not set CONFIG_XBC and CONFIG_SHA512 in rk3568_defconfig, and
include <xbc.h> in arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c only when CONFIG_XBC
is set.

In this configuration lib/libxbc (Android boot configuration) is called
from ft_verify_fdt() in board.c only, and only for an Android boot image
with header version 4 or later: for any other image the function returns
1 before it reaches that code. Without CONFIG_XBC, lib/libxbc is not
compiled and not linked, and ft_verify_fdt() only returns 1. With the
#ifdef around the include, lib/libxbc/libxbc.h is no longer read by the
build either.

lib/sha512.c was compiled, but the linker discarded all of its sections,
so the U-Boot binary held no code of it. Without CONFIG_SHA512 it is no
longer compiled.

An Android boot image with header version 4 or later is no longer
supported by this configuration: its androidboot.* arguments are still
taken out of bootargs, but nothing adds them to the boot configuration.

Incari GmbH made this change for Incari RK3568 OS, whose boot partition
holds an Android boot image with header version 0.

---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c | 2 ++
 configs/rk3568_defconfig       | 2 --
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
index 7a4124ae1e..2a74a692a2 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/board.c
@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@
 #include <syscon.h>
 #include <sysmem.h>
 #include <video_rockchip.h>
+#ifdef CONFIG_XBC
 #include <xbc.h>
+#endif
 #include <asm/io.h>
 #include <asm/gpio.h>
 #include <android_avb/rk_avb_ops_user.h>
diff --git a/configs/rk3568_defconfig b/configs/rk3568_defconfig
index db14f5e150..af9667c955 100644
--- a/configs/rk3568_defconfig
+++ b/configs/rk3568_defconfig
@@ -208,8 +208,6 @@ CONFIG_SPL_RSA=y
 CONFIG_RSA_N_SIZE=0x200
 CONFIG_RSA_E_SIZE=0x10
 CONFIG_RSA_C_SIZE=0x20
-CONFIG_XBC=y
-CONFIG_SHA512=y
 CONFIG_LZ4=y
 CONFIG_LZMA=y
 CONFIG_SPL_GZIP=y
